Assassin's Creed Valhalla's a Viking  setting is confirmed but that's not all  we know here are the important details  about the new game story characters and  launch platforms like PS 5 and series X  Valhalla is set in the 9th century at  the height of the Viking Age your clan  has been driven out of Norway leaving  them to seek shelter elsewhere the clan  is led by a boar who can be either male  or female much like how Odyssey let you  choose between Alexios or Cassandra in  fact Valhalla's modern-day storyline  with Laila picks up right after the  cliffhanger ending of odyssey's fate of  Atlantis DLC a VARs role in Valhalla is  somewhat similar to Edwards in Black  Flag like Edward a vork comes across the  assassin Templar conflict rather than  inherits it from birth as shown in the  trailer Valhalla's bird of choice is a  raven rather than the standard eagle the  assassins lean towards it makes sense  given the setting and Norse mythology  Odin uses his many Ravens to spy on his  enemies that might bring another recent  Norse adventure God of War to mind but  Ubisoft isn't worried about that  comparison we spoke to narrative  director Darby McDevitt about this and  he said it's Valhalla's grounded  historical experience that sets it apart  quote I think the urge is to always  immediately lead with the mythology  stuff but we really want you to feel  like you're living in the dark ages of  England that you're exploring the ruins  left behind 400 to 500 years earlier by  the Romans and the remnants of the  Britannic tribes before that and even  the Saxon pagans before they all  converted to Christianity that grounded  history can be seen in the game's  antagonists - the trailer shows King  Alfred of Wessex one of many leaders who  oppose the Viking forces but King Alfred  is just one villain he's not the game's  main bad guy McDevitt said Ubisoft wants  to save that reveal for later if this  info is enough to get you to pre-order  the game then you should know it has  four different editions in the works the  collector's edition does have a pretty  sweet-looking a horse statue you can get  all the pricing information on that  through GameSpot's pre-order guide as  for when Valhalla launches it's coming  to ps4 PS 5 Xbox one see  sex and PC via the epic game store this  holiday  [Music]
 

